spec:
  grid: 13x13, black background
  markers: exactly 3 single-pixel markers on distinct rows and distinct columns
    red: route start
    yellow: waypoint (bend)
    green: route end
  separation: pairwise manhattan distance 11-13 between all marker pairs [observed]
  edge_distance: each marker 1-2 cells from nearest grid edge [observed]
  input: only the 3 marker pixels on black background
  output: preserve markers; draw grey L-shaped path for each leg using horizontal-first routing
    leg1: red -> yellow, move horizontally to yellow's column then vertically to yellow's row
    leg2: yellow -> green, same horizontal-first routing
    paint only black cells grey; overlapping path cells painted once
  path_stats: each leg has manhattan length 11-13, always has both H and V component (1 turn per leg)

generation_strategy:
